1
00:00:01,035 --> 00:00:04,205
* In the not-too-distant 
 future *

2
00:00:04,205 --> 00:00:07,208
* Way down in Deep 13

3
00:00:07,208 --> 00:00:10,544
* Dr. Forrester 
 and TV's Frank *

4
00:00:10,544 --> 00:00:13,247
* Were hatching 
 an evil scheme *

5
00:00:13,247 --> 00:00:16,317
* They hired a temp 
 by the name of Mike *

6
00:00:16,317 --> 00:00:19,487
* Just a regular Joe 
 they didn't like *

7
00:00:19,487 --> 00:00:22,723
* Their experiment 
 needed a good test case *

8
00:00:22,723 --> 00:00:24,592
* So they conked him 
 on the noggin *

9
00:00:24,592 --> 00:00:26,394
* And they shot him 
 into space *

10
00:00:26,394 --> 00:00:28,796
Get me down!

11
00:00:28,796 --> 00:00:32,233
* We'll send him 
 cheesy movies *

12
00:00:32,233 --> 00:00:35,103
- * The worst we can find  
 - * La la la

13
00:00:35,103 --> 00:00:38,506
* He'll have to sit 
 and watch them all *

14
00:00:38,506 --> 00:00:41,575
* And we'll monitor 
 his mind *

15
00:00:41,575 --> 00:00:44,745
* Now keep in mind 
 Mike can't control *

16
00:00:44,745 --> 00:00:46,714
* When the movies 
 begin or end *

17
00:00:46,714 --> 00:00:48,015
* La la la

18
00:00:48,015 --> 00:00:50,651
* He'll try to keep 
 his sanity *

19
00:00:50,651 --> 00:00:55,723
* With the help 
 of his robot friends *

20
00:00:55,723 --> 00:00:57,425
Robot roll call.

21
00:00:57,425 --> 00:00:58,659
- Cambot. 
 - Show yourself.

22
00:00:58,659 --> 00:00:59,927
- Gypsy. 
 - I'm not ready!

23
00:00:59,927 --> 00:01:01,462
- Tom Servo. 
 - Hello there!

24
00:01:01,462 --> 00:01:03,030
- Croooow! 
 - That's one "O".

25
00:01:03,030 --> 00:01:06,434
* If you're wondering 
 how he eats and breathes *

26
00:01:06,434 --> 00:01:09,437
- * And other science facts  
 - * La la la

27
00:01:09,437 --> 00:01:12,473
* Just repeat to yourself 
 it's just a show *

28
00:01:12,473 --> 00:01:15,776
* I should really 
 just relax *

29
00:01:15,776 --> 00:01:20,848
* For "Mystery Science 
 Theater 3000" *

30
00:01:35,629 --> 00:01:37,131
Whoa, whoa. Hold it
right there, fella.

31
00:01:37,131 --> 00:01:38,299
Come back here
and sign in, please.

32
00:01:38,299 --> 00:01:39,300
Hey, what's up, Servo?

33
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:40,334
Sorry. Company policy.

34
00:01:40,334 --> 00:01:41,869
What? Since when?

35
00:01:41,869 --> 00:01:43,971
Since things
have been getting
too darn lax around here.

36
00:01:43,971 --> 00:01:45,973
You realize just about
anybody can walk up here

37
00:01:45,973 --> 00:01:47,308
on the Satellite Of Love
here and wander around?

38
00:01:47,308 --> 00:01:49,143
But I live here.

39
00:01:49,143 --> 00:01:50,644
You can't expect me
to keep track of every
face that walks--

40
00:01:50,644 --> 00:01:53,481
Let me just drop
these Mole Man comics
off with Crow.

41
00:01:53,481 --> 00:01:54,982
- I'll be right back.
- Now hold on a second.

42
00:01:54,982 --> 00:01:56,484
- ( beep ) 
- Hello. Crow?

43
00:01:56,484 --> 00:01:58,486
- What? 
- Uh, we got a, uh--

44
00:01:58,486 --> 00:02:00,488
Mike Nelson.

45
00:02:00,488 --> 00:02:02,323
We got a Mike Nelson
up here.

46
00:02:02,323 --> 00:02:04,158
You expecting him down there
on that side of the ship?

47
00:02:04,158 --> 00:02:06,660
Nelson. 
 Uh, yeah. Yeah.

48
00:02:06,660 --> 00:02:08,829
Huh. Well,
sign in, please.

49
00:02:08,829 --> 00:02:09,897
Sign in, too.
All right.

50
00:02:09,897 --> 00:02:10,998
Don't forget the time.

51
00:02:10,998 --> 00:02:12,666
- And that's--
- 11:43.

52
00:02:12,666 --> 00:02:14,335
11:43.

53
00:02:14,335 --> 00:02:15,336
Okay.
I'll just drop
these off.

54
00:02:15,336 --> 00:02:16,337
I'll be right back.

55
00:02:16,337 --> 00:02:17,438
Crow, here you go.

56
00:02:17,438 --> 00:02:18,672
- All right.
- ( Tom Servo mutters )

57
00:02:18,672 --> 00:02:20,508
Whoa! Sign out, will you?

58
00:02:20,508 --> 00:02:22,176
Oh, come on.
This is ridiculous.

59
00:02:22,176 --> 00:02:23,177
Company policy.

60
00:02:23,177 --> 00:02:24,678
We'll be right back.

61
00:02:24,678 --> 00:02:27,348
11:43--
wait. 11: 44.

62
00:02:27,348 --> 00:02:28,582
11:44.

63
00:02:34,188 --> 00:02:37,191
( snoring )

64
00:02:37,191 --> 00:02:38,692
I think we better
wake him up.

65
00:02:38,692 --> 00:02:40,861
He did a couple
back-to-back shifts.

66
00:02:40,861 --> 00:02:42,696
- Servo!
- Aah! Red alert!

67
00:02:42,696 --> 00:02:43,964
Red alert!
Send backup!

68
00:02:43,964 --> 00:02:46,700
Someone's breaking into
the vending machine!

69
00:02:46,700 --> 00:02:48,869
And to think
he's getting $4.35 an hour.

70
00:02:48,869 --> 00:02:50,003
Yeah.

71
00:02:50,003 --> 00:02:52,273
- Ponch and Jon are calling.
- Ooh, hey!

72
00:02:52,273 --> 00:02:54,875
* Clay looks better
in a sweater *

73
00:02:54,875 --> 00:02:57,044
* Washed in...

74
00:02:57,044 --> 00:03:02,383
Let's see.
Put the white cottons
in with the denim.

75
00:03:02,383 --> 00:03:04,885
Where is that
silk dress anyway?

76
00:03:04,885 --> 00:03:07,721
Put the towels
in with the woolens.

77
00:03:07,721 --> 00:03:10,224
And what's this here?

78
00:03:10,224 --> 00:03:11,892
What?

79
00:03:11,892 --> 00:03:14,228
Oh, Nelson.
Come on in.

80
00:03:14,228 --> 00:03:16,063
Laundry day down here--

81
00:03:16,063 --> 00:03:20,067
once a year,
whether there's
a full load or not.

82
00:03:20,067 --> 00:03:22,903
Where was I?
Oh, yes!

83
00:03:22,903 --> 00:03:25,739
Have you noticed
that coffee houses
are all the rage?

84
00:03:25,739 --> 00:03:28,242
Well, I've observed
that coffee houses

85
00:03:28,242 --> 00:03:31,245
are bursting at the seams
with pretentiousness.

86
00:03:31,245 --> 00:03:33,914
Therefore, you can't
even be in a coffee house

87
00:03:33,914 --> 00:03:35,916
and not be pretentious.

88
00:03:35,916 --> 00:03:38,419
Now to prove it to you,
the unbeliever,

89
00:03:38,419 --> 00:03:42,423
I've sent along up
some of the trappings
for a coffee house--

90
00:03:42,423 --> 00:03:44,258
surly waitress
not included.

91
00:03:44,258 --> 00:03:47,261
Clay, where are
your fine washables?

92
00:03:47,261 --> 00:03:51,599
I know I bought
you more underpants
than we have here.

93
00:03:51,599 --> 00:03:53,501
Give me that.

94
00:03:57,271 --> 00:03:59,773
Oh, come on.
I think we can be
in a coffee house

95
00:03:59,773 --> 00:04:01,108
without becoming
pretentious.

96
00:04:01,108 --> 00:04:02,610
Sure!
Don't worry, Mike.

97
00:04:02,610 --> 00:04:04,278
We'll just sit here
and prove them wrong.

98
00:04:04,278 --> 00:04:05,446
I don't feel a thing.

99
00:04:05,446 --> 00:04:07,348
Yeah, it's definitely 
not working.

100
00:04:10,951 --> 00:04:14,955
I've been recording
my life in pastels.

101
00:04:14,955 --> 00:04:16,790
The only question
worth asking

102
00:04:16,790 --> 00:04:19,960
is what am I going
through right now?

103
00:04:19,960 --> 00:04:24,632
You, the white male,
are my personal oppressor.

104
00:04:24,632 --> 00:04:25,633
Oh, my!

105
00:04:25,633 --> 00:04:28,802
Yes, yes!
She is so great!

106
00:04:28,802 --> 00:04:33,307
I saw her one-woman show.
Her soul cried out to me.

107
00:04:33,307 --> 00:04:36,977
So I'll take my rage
and box it up,

108
00:04:36,977 --> 00:04:39,480
and take it out
with the trash!

109
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:40,648
- Thank you.
- Fantastic.

110
00:04:40,648 --> 00:04:42,149
Thanks a lot,
Dr. Forrester.

111
00:04:42,149 --> 00:04:43,817
See what you've done?

112
00:04:43,817 --> 00:04:45,986
You've turned my robots
into self-absorbed
little "poseurs."

113
00:04:45,986 --> 00:04:49,323
A white male
middle-class power-holder
would say that, Mike.

114
00:04:49,323 --> 00:04:50,991
- I'm not a white male--
- Fascist.

115
00:04:50,991 --> 00:04:52,326
- Pig!
- Tell him, sister.

116
00:04:55,162 --> 00:04:57,164
Hoo, hoo, hoo!
Booga, booga, ha!

117
00:04:57,164 --> 00:05:00,501
Pardon my revelry,
put I proved once again

118
00:05:00,501 --> 00:05:04,672
that Dr. Clayton Forrester
is right, right, right!

119
00:05:04,672 --> 00:05:07,007
Well, your movie
this week, Cowsills,

120
00:05:07,007 --> 00:05:09,510
is called
"The Creeping Terror,"

121
00:05:09,510 --> 00:05:12,680
and I just know
you'll hate it.

122
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:13,847
Thank you!

123
00:05:13,847 --> 00:05:15,849
Hey, I'll show you
creeping terrors.

124
00:05:15,849 --> 00:05:18,719
These grass stains!

125
00:05:18,719 --> 00:05:20,688
Well, don't you
get it, Mike?

126
00:05:20,688 --> 00:05:23,190
The fact that we can
acknowledge our own
pretentiousness

127
00:05:23,190 --> 00:05:25,526
says something
about us as artists.

128
00:05:25,526 --> 00:05:26,694
We're not artists.

129
00:05:26,694 --> 00:05:29,029
Well, maybe you're not,
Michael.

130
00:05:29,029 --> 00:05:30,364
I don't think
any of us--

131
00:05:30,364 --> 00:05:31,699
we got movie sign!

132
00:05:31,699 --> 00:05:34,267
Oh, this thing.
Yes, I suppose I'll run.

133
00:05:46,547 --> 00:05:49,049
Oh, and now this.

134
00:05:49,049 --> 00:05:50,884
Who put hair
in the sink?

135
00:05:50,884 --> 00:05:52,052
That was me.

136
00:05:52,052 --> 00:05:55,556
The things I can do
with my Spirograph!

137
00:05:55,556 --> 00:05:58,726
When spiders
drink too much.

138
00:05:58,726 --> 00:06:01,294
I'm getting ready
to get so scared!

139
00:06:04,898 --> 00:06:07,067
These people saved
with MCI.

140
00:06:07,067 --> 00:06:08,602
Wow.

141
00:06:08,602 --> 00:06:14,241
This is nothing
a good wide-toothed comb
couldn't take care of.

142
00:06:14,241 --> 00:06:17,911
First transatlantic cable
got all screwed up.

143
00:06:17,911 --> 00:06:20,748
Maybe this is a doorway
to another dimension?

144
00:06:20,748 --> 00:06:23,216
Not one of sight and sound,
but of mind.

145
00:06:23,216 --> 00:06:24,418
Nah.

146
00:06:24,418 --> 00:06:28,756
Looks like the inside
of Robert Morley's nose.

147
00:06:28,756 --> 00:06:31,492
This is all I ever see
when I look into
a microscope.

148
00:06:33,761 --> 00:06:36,597
Guys, I tell you,
I want to be
filled with suspense,

149
00:06:36,597 --> 00:06:38,599
but, I...

150
00:06:38,599 --> 00:06:39,933
Tonight at
the Metrodome,

151
00:06:39,933 --> 00:06:42,603
Monster Design
by Jon Lackey.

152
00:06:42,603 --> 00:06:44,171
Then Gogo
the Gorilla.

153
00:06:47,608 --> 00:06:50,944
Oh, no. Kopp.

154
00:06:50,944 --> 00:06:52,279
You know, a steady diet
of staccato

155
00:06:52,279 --> 00:06:54,615
is a bit nauseating.

156
00:06:54,615 --> 00:06:57,017
Don't forget
the Phillips'.

157
00:06:59,620 --> 00:07:02,523
A.J.-- "A Jerk".
Heh heh.

158
00:07:05,793 --> 00:07:07,528
The point of view
of Helen Keller.

159
00:07:10,297 --> 00:07:11,565
Why, it's not
creeping.

160
00:07:11,565 --> 00:07:13,534
This terror
is clipping along
just fine.

161
00:07:14,968 --> 00:07:18,806
A very uninvolving
video game, this.

162
00:07:18,806 --> 00:07:22,476
I get carsick when
I'm not in front.

163
00:07:22,476 --> 00:07:26,480
Darkness at
the edge of town,
all over town.

164
00:07:26,480 --> 00:07:30,150
Boy, am I terrified.

165
00:07:30,150 --> 00:07:31,652
You must be dead,
honey,

166
00:07:31,652 --> 00:07:34,488
after driving
all night.

167
00:07:34,488 --> 00:07:35,823
What time is it?

168
00:07:35,823 --> 00:07:37,658
It's time for you
to get a breath mint.

169
00:07:37,658 --> 00:07:39,660
Almost 4:30.

170
00:07:39,660 --> 00:07:42,329
Wake up,
little Susie.

171
00:07:42,329 --> 00:07:44,665
We should be home
in another hour.

172
00:07:44,665 --> 00:07:46,800
Narrator:
 This man's name 
 is Martin Gordon.

173
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:48,001
He'll be home
in an hour.

174
00:07:48,001 --> 00:07:49,503
The lovely girl 
 beside him is Brett,

175
00:07:49,503 --> 00:07:51,739
his bride of two 
 wonderful weeks.

176
00:07:51,739 --> 00:07:53,607
They have everything.
I have nothing!

177
00:07:53,607 --> 00:07:55,876
It's late August. 
 They're returning 
 from their honeymoon

178
00:07:55,876 --> 00:08:00,013
to their home 
 in quiet, peaceful 
 Angel County, California.

179
00:08:00,013 --> 00:08:02,182
Yes, they did
the nasty.

180
00:08:02,182 --> 00:08:04,351
Martin's uncle Ben 
 is sheriff of Angel County,

181
00:08:04,351 --> 00:08:06,186
and Martin is 
 his senior deputy.

182
00:08:06,186 --> 00:08:07,420
Well, I'm impressed.

183
00:08:07,420 --> 00:08:10,023
Martin has high hopes 
 of succeeding his uncle

184
00:08:10,023 --> 00:08:11,191
when Ben retires.

185
00:08:11,191 --> 00:08:12,526
Creeping nepotism.

186
00:08:12,526 --> 00:08:14,528
But for now, 
 Martin has only 
 the thoughts,

187
00:08:14,528 --> 00:08:17,197
emotions, and pride 
 of a very happy

188
00:08:17,197 --> 00:08:18,532
newly married young man.

189
00:08:18,532 --> 00:08:20,367
He told me so.

190
00:08:20,367 --> 00:08:22,970
Brett is his, 
 and he feels no man 
 could ask for more.

191
00:08:22,970 --> 00:08:25,038
Now without warning,

192
00:08:25,038 --> 00:08:27,708
there honeymoon 
 was to become a nightmare.

193
00:08:27,708 --> 00:08:29,543
Her mother showed up!

194
00:08:29,543 --> 00:08:31,712
Boom!

195
00:08:31,712 --> 00:08:35,048
Shortly, here,
the nightmare
will begin.

196
00:08:35,048 --> 00:08:36,617
It will be soon now.

197
00:08:36,617 --> 00:08:37,718
Nightmare time.

198
00:08:37,718 --> 00:08:39,887
Oh, Martin!

199
00:08:39,887 --> 00:08:41,889
Ignition was
a little early, but--

200
00:08:41,889 --> 00:08:43,390
...saw the glowing 
 rocket descend

201
00:08:43,390 --> 00:08:46,059
in the early morning skies.

202
00:08:46,059 --> 00:08:47,895
It was reported 
 to the sheriff's office

203
00:08:47,895 --> 00:08:50,731
by Jeff, the county 
 forest ranger.

204
00:08:50,731 --> 00:08:52,733
Jeff reported 
 to Sheriff Ben

205
00:08:52,733 --> 00:08:54,602
that a plane had crashed 
 near Willow Creek

206
00:08:54,602 --> 00:08:56,904
and that he was going out 
 to investigate.

207
00:08:56,904 --> 00:08:58,138
Bob Dole!

208
00:08:58,138 --> 00:09:00,073
...would join him 
 as soon as possible.

209
00:09:00,073 --> 00:09:02,242
Barney, 
 Ben's junior deputy,

210
00:09:02,242 --> 00:09:03,577
was to summon medical aid

211
00:09:03,577 --> 00:09:05,412
and to see if 
 he could rouse someone

212
00:09:05,412 --> 00:09:07,648
at the air authority 
 in San Francisco.

213
00:09:07,648 --> 00:09:09,416
Barney smoked
in the garage,

214
00:09:09,416 --> 00:09:10,483
and look what happened.

215
00:09:12,419 --> 00:09:14,755
Meanwhile, the bride
made her first meal.

216
00:09:14,755 --> 00:09:16,256
Heh heh.

217
00:09:16,256 --> 00:09:18,592
Oh, you.

218
00:09:18,592 --> 00:09:20,794
Is the band
tuning up?

219
00:09:20,794 --> 00:09:21,929
With ionization?

220
00:09:21,929 --> 00:09:24,097
Now that we need
a narrator, he clams up.

221
00:09:24,097 --> 00:09:25,332
What's going on?

222
00:09:27,768 --> 00:09:31,271
Looks like
Queen Latifah's hat.

223
00:09:31,271 --> 00:09:33,774
I think a Walmart
has landed.

224
00:09:33,774 --> 00:09:37,110
Oh, God, it's
far out space nuts.

225
00:09:37,110 --> 00:09:40,113
Astro-nuts.

226
00:09:40,113 --> 00:09:42,015
It's going to
eliminate!

227
00:09:45,118 --> 00:09:46,954
Oh, look.
The spaceship is cute.

228
00:09:46,954 --> 00:09:48,622
Look at the little nose.

229
00:09:48,622 --> 00:09:50,791
While we're waiting,
I might point out

230
00:09:50,791 --> 00:09:53,293
that Angel County
has great opportunities

231
00:09:53,293 --> 00:09:55,295
for light
industrial development

232
00:09:55,295 --> 00:09:56,797
and for schools.

233
00:09:56,797 --> 00:09:58,465
A Chinese funeral
procession.

234
00:09:58,465 --> 00:10:00,300
What?

235
00:10:00,300 --> 00:10:02,636
He's from planet
Dreadlock.

236
00:10:02,636 --> 00:10:04,805
The pontiff
has arrived.

237
00:10:04,805 --> 00:10:06,707
I was afraid
the alien was
going to be goofy.

238
00:10:09,810 --> 00:10:11,144
Ooh! Man, it's bright.

239
00:10:11,144 --> 00:10:13,213
Should have brought
my Ray-Bans. Wow.

240
00:10:17,484 --> 00:10:18,652
Uh, thank you.

241
00:10:18,652 --> 00:10:20,153
Thank you very much.

242
00:10:20,153 --> 00:10:22,155
Thank you!

243
00:10:22,155 --> 00:10:24,324
Ohayo. 
 Ohayo gozaimasu.

244
00:10:24,324 --> 00:10:25,993
Ohayo. Ohayo.

245
00:10:27,661 --> 00:10:28,896
And don't come back.

246
00:10:34,334 --> 00:10:36,403
I forgot my purse.

247
00:10:38,171 --> 00:10:41,675
Geez, it's
aerodynamically perfect.

248
00:10:41,675 --> 00:10:43,677
Oh, boy.
My back is killing me.

249
00:10:43,677 --> 00:10:45,012
I came to this planet
because I heard

250
00:10:45,012 --> 00:10:46,413
they had Doan's Pills.

251
00:10:48,181 --> 00:10:49,516
He's trying
to carry off a look

252
00:10:49,516 --> 00:10:51,084
and he's just not
tall enough for it.

253
00:10:53,854 --> 00:10:55,756
Going to sneak in back
of this bush here.

254
00:11:00,694 --> 00:11:02,362
( sirens blaring )

255
00:11:02,362 --> 00:11:05,432
* Indiana wants me

256
00:11:05,432 --> 00:11:06,433
It's Uncle Ben, honey.

257
00:11:06,433 --> 00:11:09,402
Must be an accident
or something.

258
00:11:09,402 --> 00:11:10,603
Yeehaw!

259
00:11:12,372 --> 00:11:13,941
- Neat.
- Honey, not here.

260
00:11:18,712 --> 00:11:20,380
Aw, you newlyweds
are randy.

261
00:11:20,380 --> 00:11:22,382
Now stop it in there!

262
00:11:22,382 --> 00:11:24,384
There's a plane crash
down the road
a couple of miles.

263
00:11:24,384 --> 00:11:26,553
I'm going to be
a little short-handed
till help gets here.

264
00:11:26,553 --> 00:11:27,888
Pull around back of me.

265
00:11:29,723 --> 00:11:30,891
Go on about
your marriage.

266
00:11:30,891 --> 00:11:32,125
Nothing
happening here.

267
00:11:35,729 --> 00:11:40,400
* This is the Army
Mr. Jones *

268
00:11:40,400 --> 00:11:41,634
Come along,
both of you.

269
00:11:46,073 --> 00:11:48,241
Annette Funicello
wore khakis.

270
00:11:48,241 --> 00:11:49,576
Get in, honey.

271
00:11:49,576 --> 00:11:52,245
You have the right
to remain mine.

272
00:11:52,245 --> 00:11:55,248
Okay, now get out, honey.

273
00:11:55,248 --> 00:11:57,584
So, anyway,
we didn't see
much of the Dells.

274
00:11:57,584 --> 00:11:59,652
But we saw
the House on the Rock,
which was neat.

275
00:12:01,154 --> 00:12:04,424
( screeching )

276
00:12:04,424 --> 00:12:06,760
Heh. Still going.

277
00:12:06,760 --> 00:12:09,329
Well, it is creeping.
You've got to give it that.

278
00:12:11,598 --> 00:12:13,100
Well, it turns out
the creeping terror

279
00:12:13,100 --> 00:12:14,401
likes to frolic
in the fields.

280
00:12:14,401 --> 00:12:15,803
Lollygagging.

281
00:12:15,803 --> 00:12:19,773
I think
he's attracted
to that foliage.

282
00:12:19,773 --> 00:12:22,009
Power-walking
just isn't his thing.

283
00:12:24,778 --> 00:12:26,780
Hey, if it landed
right in Sunset Strip,

284
00:12:26,780 --> 00:12:28,949
he wouldn't be
out of place, am I right?

285
00:12:28,949 --> 00:12:30,450
Boom!

286
00:12:30,450 --> 00:12:31,785
I think he's
self-conscious

287
00:12:31,785 --> 00:12:35,122
about his
big old butt.

288
00:12:35,122 --> 00:12:37,124
Well, anyway,
I like being married,

289
00:12:37,124 --> 00:12:39,860
although I do wish
we'd go home at some point.

290
00:12:44,631 --> 00:12:46,133
Would you two
stop making out?

291
00:12:46,133 --> 00:12:47,968
We've got
an investigation to do!

292
00:12:47,968 --> 00:12:49,302
At the location 
 of the crash,

293
00:12:49,302 --> 00:12:51,138
the discovered 
 Jeff's truck,

294
00:12:51,138 --> 00:12:53,807
but Jeff himself 
 was not around.

295
00:12:53,807 --> 00:12:55,976
They proceeded with 
 their investigation.

296
00:12:55,976 --> 00:12:57,310
Oh, I'm the narrator.

297
00:12:57,310 --> 00:12:58,478
I was just on break.

298
00:12:58,478 --> 00:13:00,313
I hope you don't mind.

299
00:13:00,313 --> 00:13:02,315
Yep. It's a truck,
all right.

300
00:13:02,315 --> 00:13:04,217
It's in park.
It's at my port.

301
00:13:09,322 --> 00:13:13,827
County government
was just getting
organized at this point.

302
00:13:13,827 --> 00:13:15,495
Well, I don't
understand it,

303
00:13:15,495 --> 00:13:16,997
so let's start
shooting.

304
00:13:16,997 --> 00:13:19,332
They looked at the rocket 
 in utter amazement.

305
00:13:19,332 --> 00:13:22,035
That looks like
a Ticonderoga #2.

306
00:13:24,004 --> 00:13:26,173
A puzzled Ben 
 finally asked Martin

307
00:13:26,173 --> 00:13:27,440
what he made of the craft.

308
00:13:27,440 --> 00:13:30,177
Martin panicked
and froze.

309
00:13:30,177 --> 00:13:31,845
It's no airplane.

310
00:13:31,845 --> 00:13:34,014
Ben never asked Martin
another question.

311
00:13:34,014 --> 00:13:35,448
Could be
one of our missiles.

312
00:13:35,448 --> 00:13:37,517
This county
has missiles, sir?

313
00:13:37,517 --> 00:13:39,019
Or one of theirs.

314
00:13:39,019 --> 00:13:40,353
Shh. Honey, no.

315
00:13:40,353 --> 00:13:41,354
Whose?

316
00:13:41,354 --> 00:13:43,523
You could be right, honey.

317
00:13:43,523 --> 00:13:45,358
I don't think we have
anything this big.

318
00:13:45,358 --> 00:13:47,660
I know that from
our wedding night.

319
00:13:51,031 --> 00:13:52,699
Whatever it is,
it appears to have

320
00:13:52,699 --> 00:13:55,535
lowered their
intelligence level.

321
00:13:55,535 --> 00:13:57,204
If I could find
a windshield,

322
00:13:57,204 --> 00:13:59,139
I'd give it a ticket.

323
00:13:59,139 --> 00:14:00,040
I'm a sheriff.

324
00:14:04,377 --> 00:14:05,412
Where's that one guy?

325
00:14:05,412 --> 00:14:06,880
The, whatchacallit,
narrator guy?

326
00:14:06,880 --> 00:14:08,949
Hey! Buddy!

327
00:14:11,218 --> 00:14:12,719
Ben could not understand

328
00:14:12,719 --> 00:14:15,055
why the craft 
 wasn't severely damaged.

329
00:14:15,055 --> 00:14:16,623
He started crying.

330
00:14:19,392 --> 00:14:21,094
- Hmm?
- Huh?

331
00:14:21,094 --> 00:14:22,896
Wait, I've been here.

332
00:14:22,896 --> 00:14:25,232
I'm dead!

333
00:14:25,232 --> 00:14:29,036
Apparently,
Dan Blocker
had been there.

334
00:14:29,036 --> 00:14:32,072
What kind of a man-beast
would wear this?

335
00:14:32,072 --> 00:14:33,907
This hat belongs
to Jeff Peters.

336
00:14:33,907 --> 00:14:36,910
Wow. It's
Jeff Peters' rocket.

337
00:14:36,910 --> 00:14:39,246
Jeff! Jeff!

338
00:14:39,246 --> 00:14:40,747
Jeff, are you in there?

339
00:14:40,747 --> 00:14:42,415
Uh, yeah.
Can it wait?

340
00:14:42,415 --> 00:14:46,253
Martin, go back to my car
and get my flashlight.

341
00:14:46,253 --> 00:14:49,089
I'll just pout.

342
00:15:00,934 --> 00:15:03,770
So you pretty serious
about your husband?

343
00:15:03,770 --> 00:15:05,338
What's my time?

344
00:15:12,112 --> 00:15:14,281
Ben, don't go in there.

345
00:15:14,281 --> 00:15:15,548
You don't know
what's in there.

346
00:15:15,548 --> 00:15:18,618
Go, go, go,
go, go.

347
00:15:18,618 --> 00:15:20,120
I think I hear
moving inside.

348
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:22,122
Maybe he's hurt.

349
00:15:22,122 --> 00:15:25,458
I got to check
under the movie.

350
00:15:25,458 --> 00:15:27,294
Oh, yeah,
there's a big
mess under here.

351
00:15:27,294 --> 00:15:28,428
Jeez.

352
00:15:28,428 --> 00:15:31,731
Ben, please don't.

353
00:15:31,731 --> 00:15:33,900
( growling )

354
00:15:33,900 --> 00:15:35,135
( explosion )

355
00:15:35,135 --> 00:15:37,370
Ha! That old gag.
Exploding flashlight.

356
00:15:37,370 --> 00:15:39,639
Ben. Ben?

357
00:15:39,639 --> 00:15:41,141
He almost showed
an emotion there.

358
00:15:41,141 --> 00:15:42,976
( growling )

359
00:15:42,976 --> 00:15:44,744
Honey, we got to go
open the gifts
at Mom's house.

360
00:15:44,744 --> 00:15:46,079
Aah!

361
00:15:46,079 --> 00:15:49,149
- ( growling continues )
- ( Ben screams )

362
00:15:49,149 --> 00:15:50,817
Doesn't sound good.

363
00:15:50,817 --> 00:15:52,652
( screaming continues )

364
00:15:52,652 --> 00:15:55,989
Well, he probably
knows what he's doing.

365
00:15:55,989 --> 00:15:57,824
This is the worst
honeymoon I've ever--

366
00:15:57,824 --> 00:15:59,392
Oh, it's my first
honeymoon.

367
00:16:01,661 --> 00:16:04,831
I know he'd want us
to take the sheriff's car.

368
00:16:04,831 --> 00:16:06,499
Car One, calling in.

369
00:16:06,499 --> 00:16:08,668
Reporting large
steering wheel.

370
00:16:08,668 --> 00:16:10,937
I have some bad news
and some bad news.

371
00:16:14,341 --> 00:16:17,677
Here comes the Rocori
sock rabbit high school band!

372
00:16:17,677 --> 00:16:20,680
Within the hour, 
 Martin's unusual 
 call for assistance

373
00:16:20,680 --> 00:16:22,349
was answered by 
 a special unit

374
00:16:22,349 --> 00:16:24,851
led by a Colonel 
 James Caldwell.

375
00:16:24,851 --> 00:16:27,254
We're the special unit!
Hello!

376
00:16:29,256 --> 00:16:30,257
It took about an hour.

377
00:16:30,257 --> 00:16:31,758
They stopped
at Hardee's on the way.

378
00:16:34,027 --> 00:16:35,195
Let's get going.

379
00:16:35,195 --> 00:16:38,365
There is a branch.
This is not a drill.

380
00:16:38,365 --> 00:16:39,866
Let's go. Let's go.

381
00:16:39,866 --> 00:16:42,535
Move it over.
Let's get going.

382
00:16:42,535 --> 00:16:46,706
Ah, yes,
the days of rampant
military spending.

383
00:16:46,706 --> 00:16:49,209
All right, back
on the truck. Let's go.

384
00:16:49,209 --> 00:16:51,378
We push more logs
before 9 AM

385
00:16:51,378 --> 00:16:53,113
than most people
do all day.

386
00:16:55,715 --> 00:16:58,718
They popped
a little Dave Brubeck
into the tape deck.

387
00:16:58,718 --> 00:17:00,053
Just by moving that tree

388
00:17:00,053 --> 00:17:02,055
an owl has lost
its habitat.

389
00:17:07,894 --> 00:17:09,962
Rose of Sharon's
having a baby!

390
00:17:12,399 --> 00:17:14,967
Aw, somebody
took our campsite.

391
00:17:17,737 --> 00:17:20,573
Okay, guys,
don't frag me again.

392
00:17:20,573 --> 00:17:22,575
Sergeant, take one man
and check it out.

393
00:17:22,575 --> 00:17:23,576
Yes, sir.

394
00:17:23,576 --> 00:17:24,577
'Cause we're
special!

395
00:17:24,577 --> 00:17:26,746
Okay.

396
00:17:26,746 --> 00:17:28,981
Should we go?
I think he wants
us to go.

397
00:17:31,251 --> 00:17:32,652
I'm a'scared.

398
00:17:36,256 --> 00:17:37,424
I'll go first.

399
00:17:37,424 --> 00:17:38,591
After he's done
eating me,

400
00:17:38,591 --> 00:17:39,759
Joe, you go in.

401
00:17:39,759 --> 00:17:41,661
Sooner or later,
indigestion
will set in.

402
00:17:45,098 --> 00:17:47,667
More troops are sent in
to fix the manifold.

403
00:17:50,937 --> 00:17:54,241
( smacking lips,
grunting )

404
00:17:54,241 --> 00:17:57,877
Ah, the original concept
for the Iwo Jima sculpture.

405
00:17:57,877 --> 00:18:00,780
( beeping )

406
00:18:00,780 --> 00:18:01,948
They're going
to force Earthlings

407
00:18:01,948 --> 00:18:03,450
to read their
gas meters.

408
00:18:03,450 --> 00:18:07,019
( beeping )

409
00:18:08,788 --> 00:18:11,691
Great, a race
of ham radio operators.

410
00:18:12,959 --> 00:18:15,662
Yes, this can
all be yours!

411
00:18:17,464 --> 00:18:19,466
( beeping )

412
00:18:19,466 --> 00:18:22,202
Well, they've
perfected the dial.

413
00:18:24,337 --> 00:18:26,639
Are we inside
Television City?

414
00:18:26,639 --> 00:18:29,309
I think so.

415
00:18:29,309 --> 00:18:32,979
And back again, in case
we missed anything.

416
00:18:32,979 --> 00:18:34,814
The prices
on these Kenwoods.

417
00:18:34,814 --> 00:18:36,816
The aliens
must be insane!

418
00:18:36,816 --> 00:18:38,318
( growling )

419
00:18:38,318 --> 00:18:39,886
It's conglomerate rock!

420
00:18:41,821 --> 00:18:43,890
Oh, please.
Just five more
minutes, Mom.

421
00:18:46,993 --> 00:18:48,495
If there's
a whole bunch of
dials in there,

422
00:18:48,495 --> 00:18:49,629
I'll be so jealous.

423
00:18:49,629 --> 00:18:51,831
There's the alien!
Shoot him!

424
00:18:51,831 --> 00:18:54,000
( imitating gunshots )

425
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:55,502
The sergeant  
 reported seeing

426
00:18:55,502 --> 00:18:57,170
an amazingly large creature

427
00:18:57,170 --> 00:18:59,339
in the aft section 
 of the strange craft.

428
00:18:59,339 --> 00:19:00,673
He thought it was
Boog Powell.

429
00:19:00,673 --> 00:19:02,342
He further reported 
 that it was secured

430
00:19:02,342 --> 00:19:04,611
by a kind of 
 metal harness

431
00:19:04,611 --> 00:19:07,347
but that the creature 
 could still move 
 around somewhat,

432
00:19:07,347 --> 00:19:10,183
and for that reason, 
 they had not gotten 
 too close to it.

433
00:19:10,183 --> 00:19:11,351
Plus,
they're yellow.

434
00:19:11,351 --> 00:19:13,186
There was no trace 
 of either Ben or Jack.

435
00:19:13,186 --> 00:19:14,521
Or Akbar.

436
00:19:14,521 --> 00:19:16,022
The colonel ordered 
 continuous guard duty

437
00:19:16,022 --> 00:19:18,358
around the spaceship, 
 and decided to set up

438
00:19:18,358 --> 00:19:20,360
a temporary 
 military headquarters

439
00:19:20,360 --> 00:19:22,028
at the sheriff's 
 office in town.

440
00:19:22,028 --> 00:19:24,697
It was a brilliant
strategic maneuver.

441
00:19:24,697 --> 00:19:26,933
Yes, sir.
Jag-off.

442
00:19:28,535 --> 00:19:30,870
Back at the high school,
shop class was cancelled.

443
00:19:30,870 --> 00:19:32,539
By the next day,

444
00:19:32,539 --> 00:19:34,207
Colonel Caldwell 
 had the situation 
 well in hand.

445
00:19:34,207 --> 00:19:35,708
k.d. lang.

446
00:19:35,708 --> 00:19:38,044
He had called Washington 
 and received his orders

447
00:19:38,044 --> 00:19:39,712
from the highest 
 possible authority.

448
00:19:39,712 --> 00:19:40,880
God.

449
00:19:40,880 --> 00:19:42,715
He was to maintain 
 tight security

450
00:19:42,715 --> 00:19:45,218
and to await the arrival 
 of a Dr. Bradford

451
00:19:45,218 --> 00:19:46,886
who had been on assignment

452
00:19:46,886 --> 00:19:50,056
at the Jodrell Bank 
 Radio Observatory 
 in England.

453
00:19:50,056 --> 00:19:51,891
Upon arrival,

454
00:19:51,891 --> 00:19:54,060
Bradford was to take 
 complete charge 
 of the operation.

455
00:19:54,060 --> 00:19:56,363
* Constant
craving *

456
00:19:56,363 --> 00:19:57,564
...the world's leading 
 authority on space emissions

457
00:19:57,564 --> 00:19:58,898
Ugh.

458
00:19:58,898 --> 00:20:00,066
and had worked out 
 a series of systems

459
00:20:00,066 --> 00:20:01,234
that might lead 
 to communication

460
00:20:01,234 --> 00:20:03,636
with other forms 
 of life when,

461
00:20:03,636 --> 00:20:05,905
as, and if they 
 were contacted.

462
00:20:05,905 --> 00:20:06,906
Preposition city.

463
00:20:06,906 --> 00:20:08,275
Martin was outraged

464
00:20:08,275 --> 00:20:10,076
by the government's 
 intellectual approach

465
00:20:10,076 --> 00:20:11,744
to a monster 
 that had already killed

466
00:20:11,744 --> 00:20:14,414
and caused the disappearance 
 of his two close friends.

467
00:20:14,414 --> 00:20:16,215
Not since the Lincoln-
Douglas debate...

468
00:20:16,215 --> 00:20:17,950
Caldwell tended 
 to agree with him,

469
00:20:17,950 --> 00:20:19,752
but stated that he 
 had to follow his orders.

470
00:20:19,752 --> 00:20:21,588
It was a real
interesting
conversation.

471
00:20:21,588 --> 00:20:23,590
One of those orders 
 was to suppress the news

472
00:20:23,590 --> 00:20:25,758
of the deaths 
 of Ben and Jeff.

473
00:20:25,758 --> 00:20:28,027
Martin was appointed 
 temporary sheriff

474
00:20:28,027 --> 00:20:30,930
and all news intended 
 for public consumption

475
00:20:30,930 --> 00:20:32,265
was to emanate 
 from his office.

476
00:20:32,265 --> 00:20:33,600
What's "emanate"
mean, sir?

477
00:20:33,600 --> 00:20:35,602
The air authority 
 issued a cover-up story

478
00:20:35,602 --> 00:20:37,103
that a plane had 
 crashed and burned

479
00:20:37,103 --> 00:20:38,938
and this was to suffice

480
00:20:38,938 --> 00:20:41,107
until the experts 
 cleared up the mystery

481
00:20:41,107 --> 00:20:43,276
of the visitor 
 from outer space.

482
00:20:43,276 --> 00:20:44,277
Then they went on
to plot

483
00:20:44,277 --> 00:20:46,145
the Bay of Pigs
invasion.

484
00:20:46,145 --> 00:20:50,783
Hey, welcome
to the show.

485
00:20:50,783 --> 00:20:52,452
In a remote 
 section of the county,

486
00:20:52,452 --> 00:20:54,120
the first of a series 
 of tragedies took place.

487
00:20:54,120 --> 00:20:55,355
Is it two ladies?

488
00:20:55,355 --> 00:20:57,223
Tragedies that would 
 have been avoided

489
00:20:57,223 --> 00:20:58,425
had the public 
 been warned.

490
00:20:58,425 --> 00:21:00,793
( growling )

491
00:21:00,793 --> 00:21:04,797
* Is she really
going out with him? *

492
00:21:04,797 --> 00:21:08,768
Oh, great.
The monster's
a voyeur.

493
00:21:08,768 --> 00:21:12,472
This is how all teenagers
see themselves.

494
00:21:12,472 --> 00:21:14,140
Poor kids.

495
00:21:14,140 --> 00:21:16,809
The unbearable 
whiteness of being.

496
00:21:16,809 --> 00:21:18,978
I'll be there
in about an hour!

497
00:21:18,978 --> 00:21:20,813
If you can just
bear with me.

498
00:21:20,813 --> 00:21:23,816
( growling )

499
00:21:23,816 --> 00:21:26,486
Oh, Jerry!
You wild animal.

500
00:21:26,486 --> 00:21:28,488
Eh, uh-- huh?

501
00:21:28,488 --> 00:21:30,823
Oh, my God!
It's my dad!

502
00:21:33,660 --> 00:21:34,827
We have to get
out of here, honey.

503
00:21:34,827 --> 00:21:35,862
We only have an hour

504
00:21:35,862 --> 00:21:37,497
to eat, have sex,
and then leave.

505
00:21:37,497 --> 00:21:39,832
( imitating monster )

506
00:21:39,832 --> 00:21:41,668
( growling )

507
00:21:41,668 --> 00:21:45,638
Come on, honey.
Let's crab-walk
out of here.

508
00:21:45,638 --> 00:21:47,674
Aah!

509
00:21:47,674 --> 00:21:49,509
Could you at least
not eat my bathing suit?

510
00:21:49,509 --> 00:21:51,544
It's brand new.

511
00:21:53,846 --> 00:21:56,683
You have
a kind face.

512
00:21:56,683 --> 00:21:59,519
You're lucky
you have
thick hair.

513
00:21:59,519 --> 00:22:02,455
( woman screaming )

514
00:22:04,357 --> 00:22:05,525
Well, he's not shy.

515
00:22:05,525 --> 00:22:08,695
You can say
that much about him.

516
00:22:08,695 --> 00:22:11,598
Hey, if you could
help me out by
climbing in...

517
00:22:13,866 --> 00:22:15,702
'Twas beauty
fed the beast.

518
00:22:15,702 --> 00:22:18,371
Wow!

519
00:22:18,371 --> 00:22:19,539
He's fun to cook for,

520
00:22:19,539 --> 00:22:21,774
because he enjoys eating.

521
00:22:23,710 --> 00:22:25,712
The legs are always
the last to go.

522
00:22:25,712 --> 00:22:28,214
Mm-hmm.

523
00:22:28,214 --> 00:22:30,383
Would you eat
like a human
being, please?

524
00:22:30,383 --> 00:22:32,385
This is so rude.

525
00:22:32,385 --> 00:22:34,220
Needs some seasoning.

526
00:22:34,220 --> 00:22:36,723
Last time I eat
Norwegian.

527
00:22:36,723 --> 00:22:39,726
( screaming continues )

528
00:22:39,726 --> 00:22:41,461
Earth girls
are greasy.

529
00:22:44,897 --> 00:22:46,399
Oh, wait.
It's Lent.

530
00:22:46,399 --> 00:22:47,567
I swore off girls.

531
00:22:47,567 --> 00:22:50,069
Oh, well.

532
00:22:50,069 --> 00:22:52,405
I can't believe
I ate the whole thing.

533
00:22:52,405 --> 00:22:54,407
You ate it, Ralph.

534
00:22:54,407 --> 00:22:56,075
Good going down,
but, ugh,

535
00:22:56,075 --> 00:22:57,644
then they just
sit there.

536
00:22:59,579 --> 00:23:02,482
I love you,
spaceship.

537
00:23:02,482 --> 00:23:04,250
( beeping )

538
00:23:04,250 --> 00:23:05,251
- Aah!
- Aah!

539
00:23:05,251 --> 00:23:06,252
Wow.

540
00:23:06,252 --> 00:23:07,820
It's the creeping
newlywed.

541
00:23:11,758 --> 00:23:13,593
I have no idea
what I'm doing.

542
00:23:13,593 --> 00:23:14,761
All you dials
and gauges,

543
00:23:14,761 --> 00:23:17,096
I'm in charge.

544
00:23:17,096 --> 00:23:21,568
At this point,
the director attempted
an arty sort of shot.

545
00:23:23,936 --> 00:23:26,105
That other monster
must be the opener
for this one.

546
00:23:26,105 --> 00:23:27,440
Oh, yeah,
you know...

547
00:23:27,440 --> 00:23:29,341
Danger! Danger,
Will Robinson!

548
00:23:48,294 --> 00:23:50,963
Oh, Mike, you know
that California flag,

549
00:23:50,963 --> 00:23:52,799
the one with
the goofy-looking bear?

550
00:23:52,799 --> 00:23:55,802
California grizzly bear.
They're extinct, you know.

551
00:23:55,802 --> 00:23:56,803
Too bad.

552
00:23:56,803 --> 00:23:59,672
Anyway, I was thinking,
we are many,

553
00:23:59,672 --> 00:24:02,642
and yet we are one
here on the Satellite Of Love,

554
00:24:02,642 --> 00:24:04,477
just like California.

555
00:24:04,477 --> 00:24:06,813
And so I made us a flag.

556
00:24:06,813 --> 00:24:08,147
- And, Mike--
- Yes?

557
00:24:08,147 --> 00:24:09,649
( shouts )
Hup!

558
00:24:09,649 --> 00:24:12,819
Mike, would you
help us raise it?

559
00:24:12,819 --> 00:24:14,821
Yes.

560
00:24:14,821 --> 00:24:16,989
Okay.

561
00:24:16,989 --> 00:24:20,159
I pledge allegiance
to the flag

562
00:24:20,159 --> 00:24:22,161
of the Satellite
Of Love,

563
00:24:22,161 --> 00:24:25,498
free, united,
glorious, fruited,

564
00:24:25,498 --> 00:24:29,502
that grand, bi-lobed orb
borne of the loins
of our founder

565
00:24:29,502 --> 00:24:31,838
Jacques Duperjean
Juanacapeduay,

566
00:24:31,838 --> 00:24:34,006
former claims adjuster,

567
00:24:34,006 --> 00:24:36,342
rebel with
alabaster symmetry

568
00:24:36,342 --> 00:24:38,344
and golden
dreams of Xanadu,

569
00:24:38,344 --> 00:24:41,681
once satellite
under God-- or not--

570
00:24:41,681 --> 00:24:46,352
indirigible, with liberty
and justice for all.

571
00:24:46,352 --> 00:24:48,354
- Thank you.
- ( gun pops )

572
00:24:48,354 --> 00:24:50,356
Oh, one last thing,
Michael.

573
00:24:50,356 --> 00:24:51,524
Check your nightstand.

574
00:24:51,524 --> 00:24:53,025
You'll find
a cyanide capsule

575
00:24:53,025 --> 00:24:54,360
in case we're ever taken.

576
00:24:54,360 --> 00:24:55,862
I'm not taking cyanide.

577
00:24:55,862 --> 00:24:57,697
Well, aren't you
one of us, Mike?

578
00:24:57,697 --> 00:24:59,198
Well, cyanide
goes to my hips.

579
00:24:59,198 --> 00:25:00,867
Ah, a Tory, eh?

580
00:25:00,867 --> 00:25:02,702
Outsider!
Revanchist!

581
00:25:02,702 --> 00:25:04,704
- Provocateur!
- We'll be right back.

582
00:25:04,704 --> 00:25:05,872
Do you not know
that you have

583
00:25:05,872 --> 00:25:07,206
only one life
to live of the blood?

584
00:25:07,206 --> 00:25:09,709
Give me liberty
or kill me!

585
00:25:09,709 --> 00:25:10,610
Hmmm?
Hey, my hat.

586
00:25:12,879 --> 00:25:14,046
Well...

587
00:25:14,046 --> 00:25:15,214
No. I'm not-- no.

588
00:25:15,214 --> 00:25:17,216
Red. Commie.

589
00:25:17,216 --> 00:25:18,551
While they were awaiting 
 the arrival of Dr. Bradford...

590
00:25:18,551 --> 00:25:20,386
Bradford.
Barney.

591
00:25:20,386 --> 00:25:21,888
...instructed Barney 
 on the advice 
 of Colonel Caldwell

592
00:25:21,888 --> 00:25:23,389
Colonel Caldwell.

593
00:25:23,389 --> 00:25:25,391
to plant in the local papers 
 the news that Ben and Jeff

594
00:25:25,391 --> 00:25:27,059
had taken off 
 on a fishing trip 
 to British Columbia.

595
00:25:27,059 --> 00:25:29,228
And Jeff.
Right.

596
00:25:29,228 --> 00:25:30,730
The colonel had impressed 
 the bereaved families

597
00:25:30,730 --> 00:25:31,898
Colonel.

598
00:25:31,898 --> 00:25:33,232
with the necessity 
 of maintaining secrecy.

599
00:25:33,232 --> 00:25:34,400
Hmm.

600
00:25:34,400 --> 00:25:35,902
These brave relatives 
 had agreed.

601
00:25:35,902 --> 00:25:37,236
After being beaten.

602
00:25:37,236 --> 00:25:38,137
Ooh.

603
00:25:40,072 --> 00:25:43,242
So should
we have at it
again, honey?

604
00:25:43,242 --> 00:25:47,246
Well, I think
you're a wonderful
acting sheriff.

605
00:25:47,246 --> 00:25:48,915
Despite Brett's inquiries

606
00:25:48,915 --> 00:25:51,417
about what Martin 
 had seen in the spacecraft,

607
00:25:51,417 --> 00:25:53,419
he avoided 
 specific details

608
00:25:53,419 --> 00:25:55,588
for fear of disturbing her 
 more than she was.

609
00:25:55,588 --> 00:25:56,923
What's she doing?

610
00:25:56,923 --> 00:25:58,591
If the truth were known,

611
00:25:58,591 --> 00:26:00,593
Martin was more 
 than a little 
 disturbed himself.

612
00:26:00,593 --> 00:26:01,928
Now, cough, honey.

613
00:26:01,928 --> 00:26:05,264
Shortly thereafter, 
 Dr. Bradford arrived.

614
00:26:05,264 --> 00:26:08,434
I said, Dr. Bradford
arrived.

615
00:26:08,434 --> 00:26:09,769
He was a much younger man

616
00:26:09,769 --> 00:26:10,937
than one would 
 imagine him to be.

617
00:26:10,937 --> 00:26:12,772
I have no
preconceptions.

618
00:26:12,772 --> 00:26:15,274
I'd like for you
to meet Dr. Bradford.

619
00:26:15,274 --> 00:26:16,943
I've heard
a lot about you
from the colonel.

620
00:26:16,943 --> 00:26:18,277
Nothing bad, I trust.

621
00:26:18,277 --> 00:26:19,612
Handsome, aren't I?

622
00:26:19,612 --> 00:26:21,781
Martin
and his wife were in
the original party

623
00:26:21,781 --> 00:26:23,950
that found
the fallen craft.

624
00:26:23,950 --> 00:26:26,118
I was sorry to hear
about your uncle.

625
00:26:26,118 --> 00:26:27,620
Tough break.

626
00:26:27,620 --> 00:26:29,288
Which one of us
is talking?

627
00:26:29,288 --> 00:26:32,458
Yes, thank you.
A couple hours of sleep
did a world of good.

628
00:26:32,458 --> 00:26:35,127
Bradford thanked the colonel 
 for his assistance,

629
00:26:35,127 --> 00:26:37,296
and then asked 
 to speak to Martin.

630
00:26:37,296 --> 00:26:38,798
Martin, have you noticed
how young I look?

631
00:26:38,798 --> 00:26:40,132
Bradford questioned Martin

632
00:26:40,132 --> 00:26:41,968
about everything 
 that had transpired.

633
00:26:41,968 --> 00:26:43,469
Well, we met
and got married.

634
00:26:43,469 --> 00:26:44,971
Martin did his best 
 to recall everything

635
00:26:44,971 --> 00:26:45,972
in precise detail.

636
00:26:45,972 --> 00:26:49,475
( imitating funk music )

637
00:26:49,475 --> 00:26:50,743
That two soldiers 
 that entered

638
00:26:50,743 --> 00:26:53,479
the rocket earlier 
 had been summoned,

639
00:26:53,479 --> 00:26:55,481
and Bradford hoped 
 to learn more from them.

640
00:26:55,481 --> 00:26:57,149
No, I'm only 35.

641
00:26:57,149 --> 00:26:58,484
The doctor himself 
 would not enter the rocket

642
00:26:58,484 --> 00:27:00,486
until the arrival 
 of certain equipment.

643
00:27:00,486 --> 00:27:01,821
And fresh underthings.

644
00:27:01,821 --> 00:27:03,489
From his discussion, 
 it was apparent

645
00:27:03,489 --> 00:27:05,658
that the doctor 
 considered this situation

646
00:27:05,658 --> 00:27:07,994
a magnificent 
 opportunity for mankind.

647
00:27:07,994 --> 00:27:09,662
He celebrated 
with a Chesterfield.

648
00:27:09,662 --> 00:27:11,664
He felt that 
 if he could communicate 
 with the creature,

649
00:27:11,664 --> 00:27:14,166
it might be possible 
 to advance human knowledge

650
00:27:14,166 --> 00:27:16,002
by years, 
 or even centuries.

651
00:27:16,002 --> 00:27:17,670
Or maybe
just a few days.

652
00:27:17,670 --> 00:27:21,007
The spaceship alone signified 
 an intellectual development

653
00:27:21,007 --> 00:27:23,009
far in advance 
 of anything on Earth.

654
00:27:23,009 --> 00:27:24,343
Especially these two.

655
00:27:24,343 --> 00:27:26,012
Martin asked him 
 how he intended to

656
00:27:26,012 --> 00:27:29,015
protect himself 
 from the creature.

657
00:27:29,015 --> 00:27:30,016
Bradford said 
 not to worry.

658
00:27:30,016 --> 00:27:31,350
Then he
slapped him.

659
00:27:31,350 --> 00:27:32,685
He hadn't come here 
 to be victimized

660
00:27:32,685 --> 00:27:34,854
either by his own 
 of the creature's fear.

661
00:27:34,854 --> 00:27:36,188
Go ahead.
Punch me in
the stomach.

662
00:27:36,188 --> 00:27:37,589
Come on!

663
00:27:37,589 --> 00:27:42,194
Oh, it's so fulfilling
being married.

664
00:27:42,194 --> 00:27:45,197
There.
Our one plate.

665
00:27:46,699 --> 00:27:48,167
Martin invited
the alien

666
00:27:48,167 --> 00:27:49,702
home for supper
without telling
his wife!

667
00:27:49,702 --> 00:27:51,103
D'oh!

668
00:27:51,103 --> 00:27:53,039
Martin keeps
his softball glove
above the stove.

669
00:27:53,039 --> 00:27:56,542
Okay, it's not going to
look like meatloaf,

670
00:27:56,542 --> 00:27:57,609
but it is.

671
00:27:57,609 --> 00:27:58,711
She boils it.
I don't know why.

672
00:27:58,711 --> 00:28:00,379
Ugh.

673
00:28:00,379 --> 00:28:01,781
Eh, just eat.

674
00:28:03,382 --> 00:28:05,051
She's getting
the breakfast dishes

675
00:28:05,051 --> 00:28:07,219
done just in time.

676
00:28:07,219 --> 00:28:10,556
Hi, honey.
Pregnant yet?

677
00:28:10,556 --> 00:28:12,391
I'm pretty sure
this is my house.

678
00:28:12,391 --> 00:28:13,559
I haven't
lived here that long.

679
00:28:13,559 --> 00:28:17,396
Why don't you go in
and check it out?

680
00:28:17,396 --> 00:28:20,066
You grab the stereo,
I'll get the silverware.

681
00:28:20,066 --> 00:28:22,568
Shh. Give me
the chloroform.

682
00:28:22,568 --> 00:28:24,470
Ah, the Menendez
brothers come home.

683
00:28:27,073 --> 00:28:28,574
It's nice how
they're so playful

684
00:28:28,574 --> 00:28:30,743
after the day's
murder and mayhem.

685
00:28:30,743 --> 00:28:32,244
( no audible dialogue )

686
00:28:32,244 --> 00:28:34,246
I hope she comes out
and blows him away.

687
00:28:34,246 --> 00:28:36,582
Wow.

688
00:28:36,582 --> 00:28:38,985
Love how you put
the medicine cabinet
in the living room.

689
00:28:44,924 --> 00:28:46,759
Operation
Mild Surprise

690
00:28:46,759 --> 00:28:49,261
is going
really good.

691
00:28:49,261 --> 00:28:52,832
Boy! When law enforcement
gets playful, huh?

692
00:28:55,434 --> 00:28:56,836
Oh, hi, honey.

693
00:28:59,271 --> 00:29:01,273
Boy, three days
and it's still like

694
00:29:01,273 --> 00:29:02,441
they're just newlyweds.

695
00:29:02,441 --> 00:29:05,177
The deputy
and his siren.

696
00:29:05,177 --> 00:29:07,880
Office Third Wheel.

697
00:29:07,880 --> 00:29:09,615
Aww.

698
00:29:09,615 --> 00:29:11,683
Wow. What happens
when she cooks well?

699
00:29:15,121 --> 00:29:16,688
Ahem.

700
00:29:16,688 --> 00:29:18,190
I could use
a lozenge!

701
00:29:19,458 --> 00:29:22,194
Did you bring home
your longtime companion?

702
00:29:25,631 --> 00:29:27,466
Oh, hi, Barney.

703
00:29:27,466 --> 00:29:29,802
We'll be right out.

704
00:29:29,802 --> 00:29:31,137
That's all right.

705
00:29:31,137 --> 00:29:32,138
Just take your time.

706
00:29:32,138 --> 00:29:33,472
I won't listen
or anything.

707
00:29:33,472 --> 00:29:35,808
I didn't know
we had company.

708
00:29:35,808 --> 00:29:37,476
Look at me.
I'm a mess.

709
00:29:37,476 --> 00:29:40,980
She's saucier
than this town deserves.

710
00:29:40,980 --> 00:29:42,815
Don't be impolite.

711
00:29:42,815 --> 00:29:44,316
Go get the drinks.

712
00:29:44,316 --> 00:29:45,818
Martin's lipstick
was smudged.

713
00:29:45,818 --> 00:29:47,987
Now you're talking,
honey.

714
00:29:47,987 --> 00:29:49,321
What'll you have,
Barney?

715
00:29:49,321 --> 00:29:50,656
Your wife!
I-- oh, shoot.

716
00:29:50,656 --> 00:29:52,324
How about
a bourbon and Seven?

717
00:29:52,324 --> 00:29:53,826
Coming up.

718
00:29:53,826 --> 00:29:56,328
Would you get
the Seven, honey?

719
00:29:56,328 --> 00:30:01,500
Heh. I'm a bartender
and it's fun.

720
00:30:01,500 --> 00:30:04,236
Oh, it's all gone.
How could that
have happened?

721
00:30:07,673 --> 00:30:10,943
The young couple keeps
a lot of booze on hand.

722
00:30:10,943 --> 00:30:12,678
Booze hands.

723
00:30:12,678 --> 00:30:14,680
Boy, honey, it's like
we never run out

724
00:30:14,680 --> 00:30:16,415
of things to talk about.

725
00:30:17,516 --> 00:30:19,018
And there's
your chaser.

726
00:30:19,018 --> 00:30:21,353
'50s entertaining
at its most
sophisticated.

727
00:30:21,353 --> 00:30:23,589
Back when America
was on top
of the world.

728
00:30:27,193 --> 00:30:29,195
Hey, get a load
of this clear beer.

729
00:30:29,195 --> 00:30:30,196
You had this yet?

730
00:30:30,196 --> 00:30:33,199
Barney, you should
try marriage.

731
00:30:33,199 --> 00:30:34,200
It would do
wonders for you.

732
00:30:34,200 --> 00:30:35,367
Just try it.

733
00:30:35,367 --> 00:30:37,369
My answer is...
yes, Martin, yes!

734
00:30:37,369 --> 00:30:39,705
Barney and Martin 
 had been bachelor 
 buddies for years.

735
00:30:39,705 --> 00:30:41,373
But it is love?

736
00:30:41,373 --> 00:30:42,875
Now that Martin 
 was settling down 
 into marriage.

737
00:30:42,875 --> 00:30:45,211
they were slowly 
 drifting apart.

738
00:30:45,211 --> 00:30:48,714
Barney, naturally, 
 was still dating 
 all the girls in town.

739
00:30:48,714 --> 00:30:50,049
Naturally.

740
00:30:50,049 --> 00:30:51,217
...didn't understand 
 why Brett and Martin

741
00:30:51,217 --> 00:30:52,218
didn't pal around 
 with him

742
00:30:52,218 --> 00:30:53,552
more than they did.

743
00:30:53,552 --> 00:30:54,553
They hate cops.

744
00:30:54,553 --> 00:30:55,721
He couldn't comprehend

745
00:30:55,721 --> 00:30:56,889
that married life 
 brought with it

746
00:30:56,889 --> 00:30:59,225
not only new 
 problems and duties...

747
00:30:59,225 --> 00:31:01,727
What's the narrator
talking about?

748
00:31:01,727 --> 00:31:03,295
He's way off script.

749
00:31:03,295 --> 00:31:05,064
He's a renegade narrator
on the loose!

750
00:31:05,064 --> 00:31:07,399
Boy, let me tell you,
he's nuts.

751
00:31:07,399 --> 00:31:09,902
He never plays
by anybody's rules.

752
00:31:09,902 --> 00:31:11,870
But he gets
results!

753
00:31:11,870 --> 00:31:12,939
...felt that he was.

754
00:31:12,939 --> 00:31:14,573
Hey, want to get back
to the script?

755
00:31:14,573 --> 00:31:16,575
Since time began, 
 this change 
 in relationship

756
00:31:16,575 --> 00:31:19,912
has probably happened 
 to all-- ( audio skips ) 
 in similar circumstances.

757
00:31:19,912 --> 00:31:22,748
Life has its way 
 of making boys grow up.

758
00:31:22,748 --> 00:31:24,083
Oh, yeah.

759
00:31:24,083 --> 00:31:25,751
And with marriage, 
 Martin's time had come.

760
00:31:25,751 --> 00:31:27,586
His life was now Brett--

761
00:31:27,586 --> 00:31:29,755
a life that he 
 thoroughly enjoyed.

762
00:31:29,755 --> 00:31:31,757
Let's watch them
enjoy each other.

763
00:31:31,757 --> 00:31:34,093
So are you guys
in the mood
for Italian or--

764
00:31:34,093 --> 00:31:35,594
I guess not.

765
00:31:35,594 --> 00:31:37,930
Well, I got all
the girls in town
waiting for me.

766
00:31:37,930 --> 00:31:39,098
So...

767
00:31:39,098 --> 00:31:42,568
Mmm. Barney,
don't go. Mmm.

768
00:31:42,568 --> 00:31:45,938
The other guards
don't understand you
like I do, spaceship.

769
00:31:45,938 --> 00:31:47,039
Shh. More later.

770
00:31:49,441 --> 00:31:50,442
I can't resist.

771
00:31:50,442 --> 00:31:51,944
Show the monster
a mirror,

772
00:31:51,944 --> 00:31:54,446
he goes nuts!

773
00:31:54,446 --> 00:31:56,115
I want that guy
to get partially eaten

