00:43:43,755 --> 00:43:44,990
* Da da da da da da

1029
00:43:44,990 --> 00:43:46,758
* Da da da da da!

1030
00:43:46,758 --> 00:43:50,295
* Da-a-ah da da da da
da da da-a-ah *

1031
00:43:50,295 --> 00:43:53,732
* Da da da da-a-ah

1032
00:43:53,732 --> 00:43:56,835
Mr. Martinson, please!

1033
00:43:56,835 --> 00:43:59,337
But I just want
to dictate to you!

1034
00:43:59,337 --> 00:44:01,673
* Da-a-ah
da da da da da *

1035
00:44:01,673 --> 00:44:04,409
( vocalizing )

1036
00:44:16,487 --> 00:44:19,858
Well, I'm finally
going to propose
to Debbie.

1037
00:44:19,858 --> 00:44:22,193
That's great.
Let's see the ring.

1038
00:44:22,193 --> 00:44:24,029
Oh, no!
The ring is stuck!

1039
00:44:24,029 --> 00:44:27,032
I guess we'll
have to get married!

1040
00:44:27,032 --> 00:44:29,634
( vocalizing )

1041
00:44:29,634 --> 00:44:34,205
( vocalizing )

1042
00:44:44,215 --> 00:44:45,717
But I thought that--

1043
00:44:45,717 --> 00:44:46,885
Well, I thought
that you--

1044
00:44:46,885 --> 00:44:49,721
This has all been
a big misunderstanding.

1045
00:44:49,721 --> 00:44:51,222
I love you.

1046
00:44:51,222 --> 00:44:53,892
( vocalizing )

1047
00:44:53,892 --> 00:44:56,561
So take that,
"Love, American Style!"

1048
00:44:56,561 --> 00:44:57,729
Now I hope
they have the sense

1049
00:44:57,729 --> 00:44:58,897
to take it off
the air

1050
00:44:58,897 --> 00:45:01,066
and the courage
to show this parody.

1051
00:45:01,066 --> 00:45:03,068
And they say there's
no hard-hitting satire

1052
00:45:03,068 --> 00:45:04,402
on television anymore.

1053
00:45:04,402 --> 00:45:06,404
I dare them
to show it.

1054
00:45:06,404 --> 00:45:07,572
Whoa!

1055
00:45:07,572 --> 00:45:08,740
Movie sign!

1056
00:45:08,740 --> 00:45:09,808
We got to
get out of here!

1057
00:45:22,587 --> 00:45:24,255
Come, see the monster.

1058
00:45:24,255 --> 00:45:25,924
Don't you ever miss it.

1059
00:45:25,924 --> 00:45:27,592
While on a routine call

1060
00:45:27,592 --> 00:45:30,095
to pick up instructions 
 from Colonel Caldwell,

1061
00:45:30,095 --> 00:45:32,931
Martin received 
 an urgent message 
 from Barney.

1062
00:45:32,931 --> 00:45:34,432
* I love you

1063
00:45:34,432 --> 00:45:36,768
Barney was at Willow Creek.

1064
00:45:36,768 --> 00:45:38,436
He had responded 
 to a phone call

1065
00:45:38,436 --> 00:45:40,271
from a frantic 
 Mrs. Brown.

1066
00:45:40,271 --> 00:45:41,773
* She's got
a lovely daughter *

1067
00:45:41,773 --> 00:45:44,109
Her husband 
 and grandson 
 had gone fishing

1068
00:45:44,109 --> 00:45:45,443
and were long overdue.

1069
00:45:45,443 --> 00:45:47,278
* I'm in love

1070
00:45:47,278 --> 00:45:49,114
Barney was instructed 
 to organize a search 
 party locally,

1071
00:45:49,114 --> 00:45:50,782
and to report 
 the results to Martin.

1072
00:45:50,782 --> 00:45:52,217
And to organize
a discussion group.

1073
00:45:52,217 --> 00:45:54,452
Because of security 
 regulations,

1074
00:45:54,452 --> 00:45:55,486
he was not 
 to come near

1075
00:45:55,486 --> 00:45:56,955
the area 
 of the spacecraft.

1076
00:45:56,955 --> 00:45:58,623
Or anybody's area.

1077
00:45:58,623 --> 00:46:01,459
Martin said he would 
 join Barney later 
 if he could.

1078
00:46:01,459 --> 00:46:03,862
And watch him
and his wife
make kissy-face.

1079
00:46:06,631 --> 00:46:09,200
They should put
a door on the outhouse.

1080
00:46:10,635 --> 00:46:11,970
I got to quit
doing this.

1081
00:46:11,970 --> 00:46:13,638
I can't control it
anymore.

1082
00:46:13,638 --> 00:46:16,307
I'm a sick man.

1083
00:46:16,307 --> 00:46:19,144
"Angel Sheriff,"
this fall on NBC.

1084
00:46:19,144 --> 00:46:20,645
Acting on a hunch,

1085
00:46:20,645 --> 00:46:22,647
Martin decided 
 to see for himself

1086
00:46:22,647 --> 00:46:24,983
if the monster 
 was still there.

1087
00:46:24,983 --> 00:46:26,117
It was.

1088
00:46:26,117 --> 00:46:27,318
Case closed.

1089
00:46:27,318 --> 00:46:28,653
Bradford had 
 installed TV cameras

1090
00:46:28,653 --> 00:46:30,055
inside the spaceship

1091
00:46:30,055 --> 00:46:32,323
and was testing 
 the creature's reactions

1092
00:46:32,323 --> 00:46:34,792
to sound, light, 
 electricity,

1093
00:46:34,792 --> 00:46:36,494
color, and air pressure.

1094
00:46:36,494 --> 00:46:38,396
And "The Red
Skelton Show."

1095
00:46:38,396 --> 00:46:41,166
When Martin asked him 
 if he had any luck

1096
00:46:41,166 --> 00:46:42,500
in communicating 
 with the beast...

1097
00:46:42,500 --> 00:46:43,835
He hit him.

1098
00:46:43,835 --> 00:46:45,170
Bradford confessed 
 that he hadn't,

1099
00:46:45,170 --> 00:46:47,005
but would try again 
 when certain data

1100
00:46:47,005 --> 00:46:49,674
was returned to him 
 from computer processing.

1101
00:46:49,674 --> 00:46:51,009
You like me,
Bradford?

1102
00:46:51,009 --> 00:46:52,677
It was at this time 
 that Bradford came up

1103
00:46:52,677 --> 00:46:54,345
with a frightening theory--

1104
00:46:54,345 --> 00:46:55,680
namely that the creature

1105
00:46:55,680 --> 00:46:57,849
might be a product 
 of engineering--

1106
00:46:57,849 --> 00:47:00,852
the same engineering 
 that built the spaceship.

1107
00:47:00,852 --> 00:47:02,687
And dome homes.

1108
00:47:02,687 --> 00:47:04,923
...was why some form 
 of communication

1109
00:47:04,923 --> 00:47:06,691
had not been built 
 into the creature.

1110
00:47:06,691 --> 00:47:08,359
Martin was out
of his depth now.

1111
00:47:08,359 --> 00:47:09,861
When Martin asked him

1112
00:47:09,861 --> 00:47:11,362
if this weren't 
 something to worry about,

1113
00:47:11,362 --> 00:47:12,864
Bradford said no.

1114
00:47:12,864 --> 00:47:13,865
Don't hit,
please.

1115
00:47:13,865 --> 00:47:15,233
Probably his own failing

1116
00:47:15,233 --> 00:47:17,035
at not being able 
 to establish communication.

1117
00:47:17,035 --> 00:47:19,037
I'm just
paraphrasing, here.

1118
00:47:19,037 --> 00:47:21,039
It seemed to Martin 
 that if Bradford's 
 theory were correct,

1119
00:47:21,039 --> 00:47:23,041
humanity might 
 be in grave danger.

1120
00:47:23,041 --> 00:47:24,876
From a Hoover
floor model.

1121
00:47:24,876 --> 00:47:26,544
Bradford dismissed 
 Martin's fears

1122
00:47:26,544 --> 00:47:28,046
by pointing out 
 that the creature

1123
00:47:28,046 --> 00:47:30,548
was not exhibiting 
 any signs of violence.

1124
00:47:30,548 --> 00:47:31,883
Aside from
eating people.

1125
00:47:31,883 --> 00:47:33,751
Besides, it was firmly 
 secured by the harness.

1126
00:47:35,887 --> 00:47:37,722
That afternoon 
 in Mungreeve Park,

1127
00:47:37,722 --> 00:47:39,057
a group of neighbors 
 got together

1128
00:47:39,057 --> 00:47:40,558
for a hootenanny.

1129
00:47:40,558 --> 00:47:42,560
Hoot! Hoot!
Hootie-hoo!

1130
00:47:42,560 --> 00:47:44,062
( singing )

1131
00:47:44,062 --> 00:47:46,397
And Maria taught
the Von Trapp
family to sing.

1132
00:47:46,397 --> 00:47:50,235
And Trini Lopez puts on
an impromptu performance.

1133
00:47:50,235 --> 00:47:52,270
* I am glad...

1134
00:47:52,270 --> 00:47:55,907
This is my favorite
part. Listen.

1135
00:47:55,907 --> 00:47:57,575
* As that bird...

1136
00:47:57,575 --> 00:47:59,577
There's only one stage
of grief in this town,

1137
00:47:59,577 --> 00:48:01,779
and it's acceptance.

1138
00:48:01,779 --> 00:48:04,082
* Left me alone

1139
00:48:04,082 --> 00:48:06,417
* And did not
marry me *

1140
00:48:06,417 --> 00:48:08,253
I thought
Dave Van Ronk was
going to be here.

1141
00:48:08,253 --> 00:48:12,423
He's a rip-off.

1142
00:48:12,423 --> 00:48:15,593
Come on, Evelyn.
Let's blow.

1143
00:48:15,593 --> 00:48:16,594
* I tried

1144
00:48:16,594 --> 00:48:17,929
Send help!

1145
00:48:17,929 --> 00:48:20,431
* To forget her

1146
00:48:20,431 --> 00:48:23,001
I admire
their willpower.

1147
00:48:23,001 --> 00:48:25,436
* But I'll still
think of her *

1148
00:48:25,436 --> 00:48:27,772
What a lovely
spot to get killed.

1149
00:48:27,772 --> 00:48:31,642
* Till the day
that I die *

1150
00:48:31,642 --> 00:48:32,944
( chuckles )

1151
00:48:32,944 --> 00:48:34,946
Oh, no!
The monster did
a doo-doo!

1152
00:48:34,946 --> 00:48:35,846
Wow.

1153
00:48:38,616 --> 00:48:40,118
Teehee-hee-hee.

1154
00:48:40,118 --> 00:48:42,287
These hootenannies 
just get me going.

1155
00:48:42,287 --> 00:48:43,854
Teehee-hee.

1156
00:48:46,291 --> 00:48:47,525
I'm in love,
Jim.

1157
00:48:49,294 --> 00:48:51,296
Ah, "The Young
Peter Graves Chronicles."

1158
00:48:51,296 --> 00:48:52,297
What is it?

1159
00:48:52,297 --> 00:48:53,364
Just our
impending death.

1160
00:48:57,802 --> 00:48:59,137
Oh, no. They've
wandered on to

1161
00:48:59,137 --> 00:49:00,771
a federal
monster reserve.

1162
00:49:04,475 --> 00:49:06,377
Make the leaves
go away.

1163
00:49:10,815 --> 00:49:12,483
Oh, no!
They're about
to be attacked

1164
00:49:12,483 --> 00:49:15,653
by a point
of view shot!

1165
00:49:15,653 --> 00:49:16,654
Ah, no thanks.

1166
00:49:16,654 --> 00:49:17,822
We don't want
any carpet.

1167
00:49:17,822 --> 00:49:18,990
Thank you.

1168
00:49:18,990 --> 00:49:20,391
We'll wait here
while you kill us.

1169
00:49:23,494 --> 00:49:24,662
Watch the hair.

1170
00:49:24,662 --> 00:49:25,830
Aah!

1171
00:49:25,830 --> 00:49:28,333
Making out kills.

1172
00:49:28,333 --> 00:49:30,935
Who dare ruin
my folk fest?

1173
00:49:33,271 --> 00:49:35,173
El Kabong
will kill it!

1174
00:49:35,173 --> 00:49:37,008
You stay there.

1175
00:49:37,008 --> 00:49:39,344
Stay calm.

1176
00:49:39,344 --> 00:49:40,411
Okay.

1177
00:49:44,182 --> 00:49:46,851
Someone is finally
standing up
to the monster.

1178
00:49:46,851 --> 00:49:47,852
That's right.

1179
00:49:47,852 --> 00:49:50,421
Only Tom Paxton
can save us now.

1180
00:49:54,859 --> 00:49:58,363
Finally putting
his guitar to good use.

1181
00:49:58,363 --> 00:50:01,032
Have the Army
send in bass
and drums!

1182
00:50:01,032 --> 00:50:03,934
Years later,
Pete Townsend
would perfect this.

1183
00:50:07,538 --> 00:50:10,708
Did anyone in the '50s
ever think of running?

1184
00:50:10,708 --> 00:50:12,877
Oh, now this-- this is
outright gluttony.

1185
00:50:12,877 --> 00:50:14,712
He's depressed,
so he just goes out

1186
00:50:14,712 --> 00:50:16,047
and eats some campers.

1187
00:50:16,047 --> 00:50:18,549
( woman screaming )

1188
00:50:18,549 --> 00:50:20,285
Like a giant Popple.

1189
00:50:25,656 --> 00:50:26,891
( humming )

1190
00:50:26,891 --> 00:50:28,226
Today,
the music world mourned

1191
00:50:28,226 --> 00:50:30,895
the guy who
owned this guitar.

1192
00:50:30,895 --> 00:50:33,898
In response to a multiple 
 missing persons report,

1193
00:50:33,898 --> 00:50:36,234
Martin and Barney 
 searched the countryside

1194
00:50:36,234 --> 00:50:37,402
for the group 
 of picnickers.

1195
00:50:37,402 --> 00:50:38,569
I can fix it.

1196
00:50:38,569 --> 00:50:40,238
The only trace 
 they found of them

1197
00:50:40,238 --> 00:50:43,108
was the remains of a guitar 
 one of them carried.

1198
00:50:43,108 --> 00:50:44,742
And some
potato salad.

1199
00:50:44,742 --> 00:50:46,744
This wholesale disappearance 
 of a large group of people

1200
00:50:46,744 --> 00:50:49,580
coupled with earlier 
 missing persons reports

1201
00:50:49,580 --> 00:50:52,083
led Martin to only 
 one conclusion.

1202
00:50:52,083 --> 00:50:53,251
Folk is dead.

1203
00:50:53,251 --> 00:50:54,252
There must be 
 another monster,

1204
00:50:54,252 --> 00:50:55,420
and it was 
 on the loose.

1205
00:50:56,687 --> 00:50:58,256
The filmmakers went
back to this building

1206
00:50:58,256 --> 00:50:59,724
every time
they needed a shot.

1207
00:50:59,724 --> 00:51:01,926
Yes, Mother. Yes.

1208
00:51:01,926 --> 00:51:03,928
The colonel listened 
 to Martin's theory,

1209
00:51:03,928 --> 00:51:05,596
and after consulting 
 with Bradford,

1210
00:51:05,596 --> 00:51:07,765
decided to call 
 Washington.

1211
00:51:07,765 --> 00:51:10,101
He was told to follow 
 his own good judgment...

1212
00:51:10,101 --> 00:51:11,102
Uh-oh.

1213
00:51:11,102 --> 00:51:12,270
but under no circumstances

1214
00:51:12,270 --> 00:51:14,439
was he to alarm 
 the populace.

1215
00:51:14,439 --> 00:51:16,274
The colonel decided 
 to organize

1216
00:51:16,274 --> 00:51:17,608
a county-wide search.

1217
00:51:17,608 --> 00:51:18,943
And bake sale.

1218
00:51:18,943 --> 00:51:20,111
Martin's assignment 
 was to search

1219
00:51:20,111 --> 00:51:21,679
the north end 
 of the county.

1220
00:51:25,116 --> 00:51:26,784
He needs
to walk faster

1221
00:51:26,784 --> 00:51:28,286
to maintain
an adequate heart rate

1222
00:51:28,286 --> 00:51:30,788
and burn off
all those calories
from those people.

1223
00:51:30,788 --> 00:51:32,123
His wife,
on the other hand,

1224
00:51:32,123 --> 00:51:33,958
can eat anything
and not worry
about it.

1225
00:51:33,958 --> 00:51:36,461
I hate her.

1226
00:51:36,461 --> 00:51:37,962
You know what
would work for him now?

1227
00:51:37,962 --> 00:51:39,464
Kind of a low-rise pump

1228
00:51:39,464 --> 00:51:40,865
rather than
those Birkenstocks.

1229
00:51:42,800 --> 00:51:44,735
I can't believe it.
I'm hungry again.

1230
00:51:47,805 --> 00:51:50,808
While Martin and Brett 
 were engaged by the search,

1231
00:51:50,808 --> 00:51:53,978
the monster 
 was moving toward 
 the community dance hall.

1232
00:51:53,978 --> 00:51:56,647
Where a close-knit
community mourns its dead.

1233
00:51:56,647 --> 00:51:58,816
( music playing )

1234
00:51:58,816 --> 00:51:59,984
Well, I assume
the authorities

1235
00:51:59,984 --> 00:52:01,319
aren't keeping
anything from me,

1236
00:52:01,319 --> 00:52:03,020
so let's dance!

1237
00:52:06,657 --> 00:52:07,992
* Yeah,
here's my torso *

1238
00:52:07,992 --> 00:52:09,994
* Torso, there's a torso,
look at torsos *

1239
00:52:09,994 --> 00:52:11,162
* Just sing
my torso *

1240
00:52:11,162 --> 00:52:12,663
* Sing her torso,
look at torsos *

1241
00:52:12,663 --> 00:52:14,999
Timothy Leary
and Estelle Parsons
get down.

1242
00:52:14,999 --> 00:52:17,502
Whoo!

1243
00:52:17,502 --> 00:52:21,172
I'm surprised
we got this
good a turnout

1244
00:52:21,172 --> 00:52:24,008
with everyone
being dead and all.

1245
00:52:24,008 --> 00:52:26,076
You know,
everyone was
forty back then.

1246
00:52:28,179 --> 00:52:30,581
Boy, these Huey Long
fundraisers are great.

1247
00:52:33,518 --> 00:52:36,254
Apparently,
the monster ate
the decorating committee.

1248
00:52:37,522 --> 00:52:39,524
Just a good thing
drugs came along.

1249
00:52:39,524 --> 00:52:40,691
I'll say.

1250
00:52:40,691 --> 00:52:42,693
This town desperately
needs a leather bar.

1251
00:52:42,693 --> 00:52:44,094
Even a dairy bar.

1252
00:52:47,698 --> 00:52:49,600
The mid-afternoon dance
is a big success.

1253
00:52:52,870 --> 00:52:56,707
* Wa-wa-wa-tubba
wa-wa-whoa *

1254
00:52:56,707 --> 00:52:58,209
Yeah.

1255
00:52:58,209 --> 00:53:00,778
You can see why
the British Invasion
was so easy.

1256
00:53:03,047 --> 00:53:05,049
* Wa-wa
whoa whoa *

1257
00:53:05,049 --> 00:53:09,053
* Buh-la-la,
oh, lady *

1258
00:53:09,053 --> 00:53:11,055
( humming )

1259
00:53:11,055 --> 00:53:14,058
There is just plain
no need for sex.

1260
00:53:14,058 --> 00:53:15,893
We'll all be just fine
without it, dear.

1261
00:53:15,893 --> 00:53:18,396
That's right.
You tell 'em,
Sarah.

1262
00:53:18,396 --> 00:53:20,631
This dance
is a tribute
to the treble clef.

1263
00:53:22,233 --> 00:53:24,635
Even the A.V. Club
laughs at these guys.

1264
00:53:26,237 --> 00:53:30,074
They dance to forget
their desperation.

1265
00:53:30,074 --> 00:53:32,743
If my deepest,
darkest despair
had choreography,

1266
00:53:32,743 --> 00:53:35,246
this would be it.

1267
00:53:35,246 --> 00:53:36,814
Sponsored
by Thom McAn.

1268
00:53:39,584 --> 00:53:41,986
Hey, no street shoes
on the gym floor.

1269
00:53:43,921 --> 00:53:46,424
Your parents
before you were born.

1270
00:53:46,424 --> 00:53:48,259
Hey, there's
a hair on the--

1271
00:53:48,259 --> 00:53:49,594
hey,
there's a hair
on the thing--

1272
00:53:49,594 --> 00:53:51,762
- Big one.
- Would you--
thank you.

1273
00:53:51,762 --> 00:53:54,332
And as ever,
the Baptists remain
on the sidelines.

1274
00:53:56,434 --> 00:54:00,271
This was the unsuccessful
pilot for "Soul Train."

1275
00:54:00,271 --> 00:54:01,939
I can see why
they need a rest.

1276
00:54:01,939 --> 00:54:04,609
Yeah. Wow.
Towel down.

1277
00:54:04,609 --> 00:54:06,010
Hey, where'd
the tablecloth go?

1278
00:54:08,779 --> 00:54:09,780
Shh. Don't bother it.

1279
00:54:09,780 --> 00:54:11,949
They're so beautiful
in the wild.

1280
00:54:11,949 --> 00:54:13,851
Oh, yes.

1281
